Performance: Payload copies into an external `IBufferWriter<byte>`, multi-segment `ReadOnlySequence<byte>` reads, growing pooled buffers and stream reads use Nino's own block copy instead of `Memmove`, in one `GetSpan` of the payload's size: writing 1,000 `int`s into an `ArrayBufferWriter<byte>` is 1.07-1.41× faster on x64 and 1.27× on Arm64 (GitHub runners: AMD EPYC 7763 and 9V74, Intel Xeon 8573C; Neoverse-N2) (#261).
